# endpoint.suite — a sibling that moves to a new subnet is found again: node2
# behind NAT, node1 and the reflector in one swarm; node1 moves, and node2
# learns its new address from the reflector's forward and links to it; then
# node1 changes its address twice within 5 s, and the final address reaches
# both siblings.
#
# endpoint-change-swarm moves node2 behind NAT and admits the reflector, and
# each move-subnet moves node1 for good, so the three end their world. It has
# a suite of its own because each VM suite is one world's worth of VM time.
bootstrap-user-software-key
adopt-node
endpoint-change-swarm
endpoint-change-relink
endpoint-change-double
